WEBVTT

00:06.006 --> 00:08.007
[theme music playing]

01:03.229 --> 01:05.982
GENIE, MAKE A WISH

01:06.733 --> 01:08.943
[guard] Someone's trying to
hack into the system.

01:09.027 --> 01:12.238
What do they want? Do we know who it is?
Russia? North Korea?

01:12.322 --> 01:14.407
[guard] They're trying to
figure that out. Hurry!

01:15.533 --> 01:16.993
[intriguing music plays]

01:20.997 --> 01:21.956
[system chimes]

01:23.166 --> 01:24.042
[chuckles smugly]

01:34.469 --> 01:36.054
ALARM

01:36.137 --> 01:37.889
TEMPTATION

01:42.143 --> 01:42.977
[gasps loudly]

01:44.187 --> 01:45.104
[pills rattle]

01:47.649 --> 01:48.650
[water pouring]

01:57.867 --> 01:59.202
-You sleep okay?
-[gasps]

02:01.162 --> 02:01.996
Let's kiss now.

02:02.580 --> 02:04.874
[hesitates] Oh, I…
I need to plant those onions!

02:05.458 --> 02:06.292
[pants]

02:08.670 --> 02:09.712
[quirky music plays]

02:13.341 --> 02:15.593
[groaning]

02:15.677 --> 02:17.387
[shuddering]

02:17.470 --> 02:18.972
Finished with the onions? Let's kiss.

02:19.055 --> 02:21.349
[shudders] But I left
that thing over there.

02:21.432 --> 02:23.935
So out of it,
I forgot to grab it. [whimpers]

02:44.956 --> 02:46.416
-[wood thuds]
-[Iblis grunts]

03:03.391 --> 03:05.518
-[gasps]
-You were looking for the coffin?

03:06.477 --> 03:09.689
-Since you found it, let's kiss!
-Wait. Hold on. You can't rush it.

03:09.772 --> 03:11.983
You know? It happens when it's right.

03:13.359 --> 03:16.571
There are rules to this.
Rules around these sort of things.

03:16.654 --> 03:18.156
-Okay?
-So what are they?

03:18.239 --> 03:20.158
Yes, well, then about those rules, uh…

03:22.076 --> 03:25.204
The first one's the weather.
Raindrops. It must rain.

03:25.788 --> 03:27.749
It didn't rain yesterday.

03:27.832 --> 03:29.626
It was the first time yesterday.

03:30.209 --> 03:33.838
For the first kiss, rules can be
somewhat relaxed, even spontaneous,

03:33.922 --> 03:36.549
but now that that's happened,
it must rain from now on.

03:38.092 --> 03:39.218
We also need alcohol.

03:39.886 --> 03:42.013
A drink before a kiss. That's when.

03:44.349 --> 03:45.600
It's really that complicated?

03:45.683 --> 03:48.436
Actually, way, way more complicated,
but I condensed it.

03:48.519 --> 03:49.938
You can put the lid back on.

03:52.023 --> 03:54.150
But you're not really a vampire, are you?

03:59.447 --> 04:00.615
[keyboard clacking]

04:01.908 --> 04:03.243
[mouse clicking]

04:03.326 --> 04:04.535
[mysterious music plays]

04:06.037 --> 04:09.165
[scoffs] Numbers have changed again.

04:10.541 --> 04:11.668
That fucking psycho.

04:14.963 --> 04:15.797
[mouse clicks]

04:16.881 --> 04:18.383
What are these other funds?

04:18.466 --> 04:20.218
KI KA-YOUNG
TOTAL ASSETS: 4,300,431,074 WON

04:20.301 --> 04:21.844
CREDIT CARDS
MONTHLY PAY: 34,074,250

04:21.928 --> 04:23.471
[mouse clicking]

04:27.225 --> 04:29.894
CHEONGPUNGHO BANK

04:29.978 --> 04:31.980
LUNCH BREAK
12 TO 1PM

04:32.730 --> 04:34.107
[bell chimes]

04:34.899 --> 04:37.568
Hey, Ki Ka-young and Choi Min-ji
were in your class at school?

04:38.444 --> 04:40.113
-Yeah.
-Their bags are pricey.

04:40.196 --> 04:41.364
They're both Hermès.

04:42.490 --> 04:45.201
She just places it on the floor. [scoffs]

04:45.785 --> 04:47.787
You two, hey. Two iced coffees, okay?

04:48.663 --> 04:51.916
[groans] Every time we break for lunch.

04:52.000 --> 04:54.627
-Great.
-Go on ahead. I'll take the usual.

04:55.253 --> 04:59.132
Looking over your accounts, you should
set up a retirement savings plan.

04:59.215 --> 05:00.800
A good way to set up for your future.

05:00.883 --> 05:03.136
I don't need it.
There's no point in retirement.

05:03.219 --> 05:05.763
[laughs] What do you mean,
there's no point?

05:06.889 --> 05:09.309
It's just that she's not interested
in low-risk stocks.

05:09.392 --> 05:11.102
She tends to invest more aggressively.

05:11.185 --> 05:13.813
Of course, yes, I understand.
Okay. [chuckles]

05:13.896 --> 05:16.399
That's good to know. Bo-gyeong,
the towel sets. Where are they?

05:17.567 --> 05:18.609
-Oh.
-They're not prepared?

05:19.902 --> 05:22.989
Bo-gyeong, why is it that you need
to be told every single thing?

05:23.072 --> 05:24.282
I'll get the towels now.

05:25.283 --> 05:27.535
Let's continue to prepare
for your retirement.

05:27.618 --> 05:30.246
Let's discuss the advantages.
Your nest egg will…

05:35.126 --> 05:37.045
[intriguing music plays]

05:39.881 --> 05:44.218
The construction is complete. You just
need to decide when you want to move in.

05:45.261 --> 05:47.805
-Do you like it?
-Yes, Papa.

05:56.606 --> 05:58.566
-Daddy! Daddy!
-[squeals excitedly]

05:58.649 --> 06:00.735
-Oh, yes, my sweet angel!
-[both chuckle]

06:00.818 --> 06:02.737
Did our smart little princess
study hard today?

06:02.820 --> 06:05.156
Of course! I'm so tired. I need a break.

06:05.740 --> 06:08.534
You know, there was a new student
in school today.

06:09.035 --> 06:10.828
-He's really cute.
-[Chang-sik] Oh, cute?

06:11.496 --> 06:13.122
You found him cute? How cute is he?

06:13.206 --> 06:15.249
-He looks like a little king.
-Oh.

06:15.333 --> 06:17.085
-So I asked where he lives.
-Yeah?

06:17.168 --> 06:19.754
-He said that big house we wondered about.
-The one that a way?

06:19.837 --> 06:21.464
-Yep.
-They live in that house?

06:21.547 --> 06:24.342
Let's go see them and bring them
our good rice cakes.

06:24.425 --> 06:26.344
We have to welcome them to our town.

06:27.095 --> 06:28.012
[both] Ah!

06:28.096 --> 06:30.473
[pop music playing faintly over TV]

06:32.391 --> 06:33.559
[gasps]

06:37.105 --> 06:40.358
So the kissing rules
are actually accurate?

06:40.900 --> 06:41.984
-[door opens]
-[gasps]

06:44.112 --> 06:47.031
Genie, tell me what tomorrow's weather
is going to be like.

06:47.115 --> 06:49.659
The weather? How would I know that?
It's a touchy subject, okay?

06:50.493 --> 06:53.371
What are you so riled up about?
I'm just asking about the weather.

06:54.288 --> 06:56.582
Hey, Genie,
what's the weather like tomorrow?

06:56.666 --> 06:59.877
[AI Genie] Tomorrow, in Cheongpung,
it's going to be a clear and sunny day.

06:59.961 --> 07:04.257
That's right. You should try asking it
something. It knows everything.

07:09.512 --> 07:11.556
[Iblis scoffs] Okay, other Genie.

07:12.348 --> 07:14.767
What does Ki Ka-young most want to know?

07:15.560 --> 07:18.729
[AI Genie] Here's a list of
Ki Ka-young's recent search history.

07:18.813 --> 07:23.109
Rainmaking rites, artificial rain,
the alcoholic content of beer,

07:23.192 --> 07:25.820
cool-toned lip tints,
express delivery action.

07:25.903 --> 07:28.739
Rainmaking rites, rainmaking rites,
rainmaking rites…

07:28.823 --> 07:31.033
What the hell have you done, you idiot?

07:31.117 --> 07:32.326
…rainmaking rites.

07:35.538 --> 07:37.540
Find out how much rain
is expected this week.

07:37.623 --> 07:40.835
I already looked it up because the cherry
blossom festival starts very soon.

07:41.419 --> 07:44.088
-We've got clear skies most of the week!
-Ugh! Why?

07:44.172 --> 07:45.089
[trunk thuds]

07:45.923 --> 07:46.966
How about next week?

07:48.509 --> 07:52.346
Uh, the spring rainy season
probably starts next week after Monday.

07:52.430 --> 07:54.640
-Why is Monday excluded?
-You want me to exclude it?

07:54.724 --> 07:55.933
Can you really do that?

07:57.602 --> 08:00.062
-Since you're a fairytale creature?
-I don't have that range.

08:00.146 --> 08:02.732
I could recite a devotion. [laughs]

08:05.193 --> 08:06.819
Not the helpful type.

08:07.403 --> 08:10.198
Why don't you put down the wrench
and tell me what this is about?

08:10.281 --> 08:11.324
[Sade exhales nervously]

08:12.742 --> 08:15.244
-You see something there?
-Yes, today I'm pretty.

08:15.953 --> 08:18.498
[Iblis humming]

08:18.581 --> 08:19.749
[stops humming]

08:20.374 --> 08:21.292
So pretty.

08:22.919 --> 08:24.712
[breath trembles]

08:24.795 --> 08:25.838
Beautiful.

08:27.215 --> 08:28.549
[panting]

08:29.383 --> 08:31.344
It's like the town got short on cash.

08:32.053 --> 08:34.138
They couldn't invite some bigwig
for the jamboree?

08:34.222 --> 08:35.473
-[metal clangs]
-Wha-- Oh!

08:36.057 --> 08:37.058
Put that knife down!

08:40.895 --> 08:41.729
I'm so pretty.

08:43.272 --> 08:44.524
All day I've been pretty.

08:45.024 --> 08:49.278
Goodness gracious, young lady!
We have mirrors all over the house!

08:50.947 --> 08:52.365
[whimsical music plays]

08:56.869 --> 08:59.330
[Sade] This isn't your fault, Master.

09:00.915 --> 09:04.835
Psychopaths are known to have
narcissistic personality traits.

09:05.586 --> 09:08.339
Is that so? Oh, that's good to know.

09:08.422 --> 09:12.260
I thought I made her pretty somehow.
I mean, I really brought it that night.

09:12.885 --> 09:15.805
[sighs] Why did I put it all out there
at that very moment?

09:16.389 --> 09:18.224
What are you going on about?

09:18.307 --> 09:20.059
You must put it all out there!

09:20.142 --> 09:22.353
Kissing is a good first step
towards corruption.

09:22.436 --> 09:24.355
Right. That's how I used to do it.

09:25.398 --> 09:27.525
[sighs] Though
it's been a thousand years.

09:28.192 --> 09:32.488
It's really been the first kiss since
that long ago. Oh, I was so nervous.

09:32.572 --> 09:33.447
[chuckles, sighs]

09:33.531 --> 09:36.158
My goodness,
it makes me feel bad for Ejllael.

09:36.242 --> 09:39.412
You know, Master, he works nonstop
in hopes of slitting your throat.

09:39.495 --> 09:43.291
He goes through all that effort when just
one kiss has you digging your grave.

09:43.874 --> 09:48.212
-Although, first kiss in a millennium?
-What's the problem?

09:48.296 --> 09:52.216
Shouldn't you have gone to
a dentist first? Ugh, so gross. Ew!

09:53.968 --> 09:55.803
-Ugh!
-A dentist?

09:57.597 --> 09:58.598
What's that?

09:58.681 --> 10:00.516
[dramatic music plays]

10:06.814 --> 10:08.566
[assistant] Any discomfort,
raise your hand.

10:10.526 --> 10:11.902
We haven't started yet.

10:11.986 --> 10:13.571
-Now, open wide.
-[shudders]

10:14.155 --> 10:15.239
[drill whirring]

10:15.323 --> 10:17.950
-[Iblis whimpers]
-Let's try to hang in there.

10:18.951 --> 10:21.579
[Iblis yelping loudly]

10:23.789 --> 10:25.833
[yelping loudly]

10:27.835 --> 10:30.588
So, you don't have any money,
or any form of ID?

10:31.297 --> 10:33.549
No one bothered to get this info
before the cleaning?

10:33.633 --> 10:36.093
He said the owner of the repair shop
was a good friend of his.

10:36.177 --> 10:39.221
Ki Ka-young? Aside from me,
she has no other friends. Oh!

10:39.305 --> 10:41.223
-You're from the Middle East?
-Min-ji?

10:41.307 --> 10:42.600
-Oh! Min-ji!
-[squeals]

10:43.559 --> 10:44.393
[Iblis] Oh.

10:45.269 --> 10:48.397
You ate gamja-tang before. I saw you
eat gamja-tang at her favorite joint.

10:48.481 --> 10:49.607
[Iblis laughs]

10:49.690 --> 10:52.401
So because you watched me
eat gamja-tang one time,

10:52.485 --> 10:54.153
you think you get a free service?

10:55.821 --> 10:56.822
[Ka-young] No money?

10:57.615 --> 10:59.075
[Min-ji] It's crazy, right?

10:59.659 --> 11:01.077
Can you believe this guy?

11:01.160 --> 11:03.329
He doesn't even have any kind of ID.

11:03.412 --> 11:04.914
He just keeps saying his name…

11:05.414 --> 11:08.334
[laughs] …is Lee Beu-li.

11:08.918 --> 11:11.420
What kind of name is that?
It's so ridiculous.

11:11.504 --> 11:13.714
What else could I say to him
at that point?

11:13.798 --> 11:16.592
How am I supposed to trust anything
about this guy?

11:17.301 --> 11:20.262
I can say one thing for sure.
He's not a real man.

11:20.888 --> 11:23.391
[Min-ji] Of course not!
There's no way he could be!

11:23.474 --> 11:26.394
No real man would date someone
when he's flat-out broke.

11:27.353 --> 11:31.065
I was told to raise these when I'm feeling
uneasy. I'm feeling very uneasy right now.

11:31.148 --> 11:32.608
Ugh, you really suck.

11:33.192 --> 11:35.611
Dr. Choi, we got to get set up
at the festival.

11:36.112 --> 11:37.196
All right, let's go.

11:39.031 --> 11:40.616
Can't you tell he's using you?

11:41.742 --> 11:44.745
Get it together!
Miss Ki, take care of yourself!

11:45.538 --> 11:47.748
[scoffs] He has a pretty face.

11:47.832 --> 11:50.126
And he's tall,
and he has a nice voice too.

11:51.085 --> 11:52.711
What else does he have going for him?

11:56.757 --> 11:57.758
[Ka-young sighs]

12:00.302 --> 12:02.513
I had to get my teeth cleaned
for the rainy season.

12:03.556 --> 12:06.058
When I become a pro gamer,
I'll pay you ba-- [sighs]

12:06.892 --> 12:07.726
Pro gamer?

12:09.019 --> 12:12.773
You haven't won a single game against the
local kids, and you think you're a gamer?

12:14.483 --> 12:15.401
All right.

12:20.656 --> 12:22.533
-[comical music plays]
-[sighs]

12:23.159 --> 12:24.618
Only one side of my face.

12:26.203 --> 12:28.122
I took that beating well. [chuckles]

12:30.082 --> 12:32.376
[mimics engine revving]

12:43.471 --> 12:45.306
-[remote clicks]
-[car engine starts]

12:45.389 --> 12:47.766
Whoa! What the… [gasps]

12:48.601 --> 12:51.562
Miss Ki! Check the tire pressure,
would you?

12:52.188 --> 12:53.063
[Ka-young] Okay!

12:53.814 --> 12:56.025
[mimicking engine revving]

13:01.489 --> 13:02.907
You having a beer?

13:02.990 --> 13:04.241
Yeah, that's right.

13:04.909 --> 13:07.620
And with the engine on,
you're at the wheel of a car?

13:07.703 --> 13:09.455
Mm-hmm. Yes, I'm behind the wheel.

13:10.331 --> 13:12.583
Engine? Which one is that?

13:13.167 --> 13:15.503
Okay, sir, go ahead
and blow into this now.

13:16.879 --> 13:18.506
What is it? A pipe?

13:18.589 --> 13:19.757
[chuckles] Come on.

13:21.133 --> 13:22.051
[blowing]

13:22.134 --> 13:23.677
-Yes, go.
-More.

13:23.761 --> 13:28.057
-[officers] More, more, more, more!
-[horn honking]

13:28.140 --> 13:29.683
-[rapid beeping]
-[sustained honking]

13:30.392 --> 13:33.562
[woman] Hello, my homies!
Hey! It's Da-jin of Sky Farm Life.

13:33.646 --> 13:36.982
I'm coming live to you from
the Cheongpung Cherry Blossom Festival.

13:37.483 --> 13:40.528
Let's start by raiding
the For Daughter Strawberry stand.

13:41.237 --> 13:44.323
What happens when strawberries
are stuck in traffic?

13:44.406 --> 13:46.450
-[man] What?
-A berry jam.

13:46.534 --> 13:48.869
[both laughing]

13:49.912 --> 13:51.205
"Strawberry jam!"

13:52.164 --> 13:54.250
[both laughing]

13:54.333 --> 13:57.211
See that? There's a reason
these things don't work out.

13:57.294 --> 13:59.964
-Great. Good. [continues indistinctly]
-Yeah.

14:00.047 --> 14:02.216
[Min-ji] Say "Ah." That's right.
Really good.

14:02.299 --> 14:04.677
[sucks breath] Let's try opening wider.
A little more.

14:04.760 --> 14:05.970
"Ah." Wider. "Ah, ah."

14:06.053 --> 14:08.097
Hello there. We're Cheongpungho Bank.

14:08.180 --> 14:11.141
We're having a promotion for savings
account. Come by for a consultation.

14:12.268 --> 14:13.102
Hello.

14:17.731 --> 14:20.859
[in Arabic] Where is the bathroom?
Is the subway station close by?

14:21.443 --> 14:22.987
Without cilantro, please.

14:23.487 --> 14:26.282
[in English] What's he saying?
Are you Arabic? Is that it?

14:26.365 --> 14:28.409
Before, you were speaking Korean properly.

14:28.492 --> 14:29.660
[Iblis] Hmm?

14:29.743 --> 14:32.454
-He's asking to leave the cilantro out.
-What?

14:32.538 --> 14:35.082
[chuckles] Arabic was all the rage
when I was in school,

14:35.165 --> 14:36.709
so I learned it as my second language.

14:36.792 --> 14:38.878
I can try speaking to him.
[clears throat]

14:38.961 --> 14:40.838
[in Arabic] My name is Oh Gyeong-yeol,

14:40.921 --> 14:42.798
a police officer
from the Republic of Korea.

14:42.882 --> 14:45.801
Sir, you have violated the traffic laws--

14:45.885 --> 14:46.802
[snaps fingers]

14:48.470 --> 14:51.307
[in English] Get over here now!
You said I just had to talk in Arabic.

14:51.974 --> 14:54.727
Oh, well, it worked for me,
but that was 100 years ago.

14:56.103 --> 14:58.063
Go ahead, I'll take care of things.

14:58.147 --> 14:59.231
-You shit!
-[whimpers]

15:03.110 --> 15:04.737
[upbeat music playing over speakers]

15:04.820 --> 15:08.532
Oh Pan-geum! Buy that,
it's yummy. That one.

15:10.075 --> 15:12.369
Why are you eating a bag of raw tofu?

15:12.995 --> 15:14.955
This is what you eat
after a visit to the slammer.

15:15.039 --> 15:19.084
Pan-geum, get black goat extract.
Black goat, okay? For longevity.

15:19.168 --> 15:22.421
How would I afford that?
Why don't you buy it for me then?

15:23.756 --> 15:26.467
Sorry, I can't afford it either.
I can only make suggestions.

15:27.134 --> 15:31.805
I can't tell if you're a rascal,
or just poor, and good for nothing.

15:31.889 --> 15:32.723
-[squeaking]
-Oh, my!

15:32.806 --> 15:34.600
-Hmm?
-Hey, hey, look over there!

15:34.683 --> 15:35.768
[toy squeaking]

15:35.851 --> 15:38.395
My goodness! That puppy's bopping!

15:38.479 --> 15:40.105
How wonderful, don't you think?

15:40.189 --> 15:42.733
-Whoa! Wow! What is that? [laughs]
-[vendor] Come and see.

15:42.816 --> 15:44.652
-How adorable!
-Super cool!

15:44.735 --> 15:46.111
[laughs]

15:46.195 --> 15:48.906
[Iblis] Wow, it's walking
but somehow stays in the same spot.

15:49.490 --> 15:50.532
How does it do that?

15:51.033 --> 15:52.826
[toy squeaking]

15:54.203 --> 15:56.080
[Iblis] At least her joints
are in good shape.

15:58.832 --> 16:00.751
-Oh!
-Hi there. So sorry, okay?

16:04.004 --> 16:04.880
What's wrong?

16:07.883 --> 16:10.010
I heard about something called fireworks.

16:10.844 --> 16:12.805
-Do you know when and where?
-[chuckles]

16:13.764 --> 16:17.226
Ah, the fireworks?
They'll go off after the sun sets.

16:18.435 --> 16:20.646
Uh, over there.
Those are the best views.

16:20.729 --> 16:22.439
-Have a good time.
-Ah.

16:23.482 --> 16:25.192
The best views are there.

16:27.319 --> 16:28.988
[humming]

16:29.071 --> 16:32.533
[music continues over speakers]

16:37.371 --> 16:39.081
[thug] Ta-da! That's it! Uh…

16:40.374 --> 16:43.752
Ah, shit. That asshole seemed like
he was loaded. All he had was this.

16:43.836 --> 16:45.421
[sighs] This is nothing!

16:45.504 --> 16:49.049
Look over there at those motherfuckers
with no decency.

16:49.633 --> 16:51.385
This is our turf.
What are you doing on it?

16:51.468 --> 16:55.472
Oh, we're here for the cherry blossom
festival. The spring breeze is good.

16:55.556 --> 16:58.475
This cherry blossom festival
is part of our turf.

16:58.559 --> 17:01.645
You didn't see us bumming around
at your salmon festival.

17:01.729 --> 17:04.398
Well, then, you're welcome
to come to next year's one.

17:04.481 --> 17:05.774
Want a personal invite, huh?

17:05.858 --> 17:09.486
Yeah. You can get a new arm
while you're here.

17:10.154 --> 17:12.072
The prosthetics in Cheongpung
are exceptional.

17:12.698 --> 17:13.907
You're gonna need it.

17:14.825 --> 17:16.243
[thugs grunting]

17:16.326 --> 17:17.995
-Whoa.
-What the hell?

17:21.915 --> 17:25.461
[sighs] Phew, what a relief!
She would've beaten me up again.

17:25.544 --> 17:27.379
-Huh? Who's this stupid prick?
-[blows]

17:27.463 --> 17:29.923
-Hey, you. What gang do you belong to?
-Huh?

17:30.007 --> 17:31.675
-Huh?
-[thug 2] Why doesn't he answer?

17:31.759 --> 17:34.470
-Hey, let's fucking wipe him out!
-[thugs yelling]

17:35.679 --> 17:37.389
-[gasps]
-[gasps, whimpers]

17:37.473 --> 17:39.475
[Iblis] My, oh, my. [scoffs]

17:39.558 --> 17:40.809
How about some flowers?

17:40.893 --> 17:43.937
[upbeat music plays]

17:44.021 --> 17:46.732
[thugs yelling, grunting]

17:50.027 --> 17:51.695
[grunts, exclaims]

17:52.988 --> 17:55.449
[both grunting]

17:58.619 --> 18:00.704
[fireworks exploding]

18:03.540 --> 18:05.375
[Pan-geum] Those are so bright
and beautiful!

18:06.210 --> 18:07.836
[Heung-rye] My gosh. How dazzling!

18:07.920 --> 18:09.963
-Oh.
-Oh, my.

18:10.547 --> 18:12.966
Oh, how mesmerizing.

18:17.638 --> 18:19.807
[indistinct chatter]

18:21.100 --> 18:22.851
[Pan-geum] Oh, my goodness.

18:22.935 --> 18:25.521
That's… that's Ka-young's name,
isn't it?

18:26.271 --> 18:29.525
"Heart. You. Live, fuck"?

18:29.608 --> 18:31.068
What? I don't get it.

18:31.151 --> 18:33.028
So that asshole does have money.

18:35.114 --> 18:37.366
So you're saying girls love
to be spoken to that way?

18:37.449 --> 18:40.994
Yes, sir. If you believe in me,
I promise I'll never steer you wrong.

18:41.078 --> 18:42.538
They all fall for it.

18:42.621 --> 18:46.083
Now it's just a waiting game
until she's corrupted. [cackling]

18:46.166 --> 18:47.042
I like that.

18:48.043 --> 18:50.295
[upbeat music continues]

18:56.844 --> 18:59.346
KI KA-YOUNG
FUCK OFF

19:00.097 --> 19:02.015
[sighs] That ass.

19:03.142 --> 19:05.978
I have that exact same thought
when I see Iblis.

19:06.562 --> 19:08.313
It's good to know you can relate, Miss Ki.

19:10.899 --> 19:13.986
Why are you here?
You don't need repairs, you can fly.

19:15.112 --> 19:17.656
Everyone's at the festival,
so this neighborhood's a ghost town.

19:18.323 --> 19:21.535
-I thought I'd visit so we can talk alone.
-What do you have to say then?

19:22.411 --> 19:23.954
No point asking for your feather.

19:24.580 --> 19:26.540
[laughs] No, it's yours.

19:29.459 --> 19:31.128
What's your species anyway?

19:31.670 --> 19:33.881
Yorkshire Terriers and Chihuahuas
are a kind.

19:34.464 --> 19:37.968
There are also angels, humans,
devils and Genies. So what one are you?

19:38.051 --> 19:41.180
Let's say I'm his servant. You saw
my wings, so you should know I'm an angel.

19:42.014 --> 19:47.060
Oh, an angel? Clarify that for me
since you have black wings.

19:48.270 --> 19:49.855
You're the food bank volunteer.

19:50.981 --> 19:52.566
I've been thinking this over.

19:53.066 --> 19:56.361
It's strange that every time
you come with meals, a life ends.

19:57.321 --> 19:58.197
Older people die.

19:58.280 --> 20:00.699
I suppose you could maybe see it that way.

20:00.782 --> 20:02.868
Mmm. Here's another perspective.

20:03.535 --> 20:06.163
I visit the elderly
who are already at death's door.

20:06.246 --> 20:07.789
It's normal some end up dying.

20:07.873 --> 20:10.834
[tense music plays]

20:13.086 --> 20:13.962
I see.

20:15.464 --> 20:17.716
By the way, several of your buildings

20:17.799 --> 20:21.136
are located within just a few blocks
of this repair shop.

20:21.762 --> 20:24.223
You also don't bother hiding
your true identity.

20:25.307 --> 20:28.560
-Are you trying to keep an eye on me?
-Oh? That's correct.

20:28.644 --> 20:31.230
I work on his mandate, to be more precise.

20:31.772 --> 20:33.523
What's that? His mandate?

20:34.274 --> 20:38.278
"If Iblis decides to bow his head
to a human, you'll then…

20:39.238 --> 20:40.739
slit your brother's throat."

20:43.700 --> 20:44.868
Thrilling, isn't it?

20:46.078 --> 20:50.415
That's why I'll do whatever it takes
to ensure that you don't fall for Iblis.

20:59.049 --> 20:59.925
It's too late.

21:00.008 --> 21:01.260
[tense music continues]

21:01.343 --> 21:02.177
What?

21:03.262 --> 21:04.888
The repair store is closing up.

21:06.181 --> 21:08.976
Ah. [chuckles]
It's that time already? Hmm.

21:12.479 --> 21:14.064
But why the sudden tone shift?

21:14.147 --> 21:17.859
Let's see. It could be that psychopaths
can't hide their irritation.

21:17.943 --> 21:21.405
Or because you're trying to kill my Genie
before I do. Or maybe…

21:22.906 --> 21:24.574
it's because I've fallen for him.

21:26.243 --> 21:28.078
Which reason is it?

21:28.161 --> 21:30.038
[tense music continues]

21:35.752 --> 21:37.963
[Ejllael] I knew it.
I was right about her.

21:39.047 --> 21:40.132
[sighs]

21:45.721 --> 21:46.972
Did something happen, sir?

21:47.556 --> 21:49.641
-I found all these--
-Get rid of all these books!

21:50.183 --> 21:53.603
-Psychopath? How about deranged?
-[books clattering]

21:54.354 --> 21:56.273
I should have known it was too easy.

21:57.566 --> 22:00.652
[sighs] The two remaining wishes
could be at risk if she's this way.

22:01.695 --> 22:03.613
I should have taken my scythe with me.

22:04.156 --> 22:06.491
I mean, she spoke to me like a child!

22:06.575 --> 22:07.826
Can you believe the audacity?

22:07.909 --> 22:10.078
-That's so disrespectful.
-Mm-hmm.

22:10.662 --> 22:12.914
You do look very young, for your age.

22:13.540 --> 22:14.374
[scoffs]

22:15.125 --> 22:16.209
[buttons clacking]

22:16.793 --> 22:18.795
Did you see the fireworks?
I did the big ones.

22:19.421 --> 22:22.299
-Weren't they cool?
-Uh, why pick those ones?

22:23.091 --> 22:25.344
-[gasps] No!
-[video game announcer] K.O.

22:25.427 --> 22:28.013
Hey, are you bamboozling me or what?

22:28.096 --> 22:30.766
-So, you were behind the fireworks?
-Uh-huh.

22:31.641 --> 22:34.186
[sighs] I wondered
what maniac would do that.

22:34.853 --> 22:35.687
Mani-- What?

22:37.272 --> 22:39.232
[sighs] Hey.

22:39.316 --> 22:42.986
-Where do you live? Show me the way, kid.
-[Min-ji] And where do you live?

22:43.904 --> 22:44.821
Show me the way.

22:47.657 --> 22:48.825
What?

22:50.368 --> 22:52.704
Overall, psychopaths

22:53.497 --> 22:55.624
hurt others, okay?

22:56.291 --> 22:57.709
To get what they want.

22:58.210 --> 23:02.380
But our dear Ka-young,
she is a bit different.

23:02.464 --> 23:05.926
Her grandma and the whole neighborhood
rallied together to raise her.

23:06.510 --> 23:08.053
Though she may not feel guilt,

23:08.845 --> 23:11.389
there are basic boundaries
she has learned to keep.

23:12.182 --> 23:13.558
Mmm.

23:13.642 --> 23:15.811
[clicks tongue, inhales] Okay, so what?

23:15.894 --> 23:18.730
So I'm saying
that I'm watching you, asshole.

23:19.481 --> 23:23.235
Ka-young has to keep
within her boundaries.

23:23.318 --> 23:25.654
And I keep her safe from any threats.

23:26.696 --> 23:29.866
Psychologically… [grunting]

23:32.410 --> 23:33.703
…or physically.

23:35.831 --> 23:37.457
I'm her knight in shining armor.

23:38.583 --> 23:40.127
You are, aren't you?

23:40.669 --> 23:44.756
All this time, I was thinking
you were a girl. Oh, my gosh. [chuckles]

23:44.840 --> 23:46.466
This is on the house. [chuckles]

23:52.222 --> 23:54.224
[both laughing]

24:00.397 --> 24:01.815
[soft music plays]

24:04.067 --> 24:05.777
[chuckles]

24:09.322 --> 24:11.158
-[laughing]
-What are you laughing about?

24:11.741 --> 24:14.202
That's the funniest thing I've heard
in 1,000 years.

24:14.286 --> 24:15.871
-[both laughing]
-[Min-ji] 1,000 years?

24:16.705 --> 24:18.165
What are you talking about?

24:19.833 --> 24:23.753
You came to a seafood restaurant
just because a guy is with us?

24:23.837 --> 24:27.299
-That's annoying.
-I only walked in when I saw you here.

24:27.883 --> 24:30.218
I'll drop Min-ji off.
Go ahead and I'll see you at home.

24:30.302 --> 24:32.929
Why don't I take her home?
We've gotten really close.

24:33.013 --> 24:36.224
-Wait, Ka-young!
-[laughs] Excuse me, sir?

24:37.475 --> 24:40.228
-Is there anything else you need?
-Mmm…

24:41.813 --> 24:43.190
-Charity?
-What?

24:43.940 --> 24:45.358
[amusing music plays]

24:45.442 --> 24:48.236
Min-ji didn't leave any cash.
And, well, I… [claps]

24:49.529 --> 24:51.448
I have no money at all. [laughing]

24:51.531 --> 24:53.158
[woman] Oh!

24:53.241 --> 24:55.243
[both laughing]

24:59.122 --> 25:01.249
Oh, I know what that is. I got it.

25:06.004 --> 25:07.672
-[line rings]
-This the police?

25:08.840 --> 25:10.133
I'm turning myself in.

25:10.217 --> 25:12.719
[distant siren wailing]

25:19.184 --> 25:20.685
You dined and dashed? Huh?

25:20.769 --> 25:22.437
[sighs] This is so unfair!

25:22.520 --> 25:24.689
I didn't really dine. I didn't even dash.

25:24.773 --> 25:25.815
Will you shut it?

25:26.399 --> 25:30.153
Why call me to bail you out? And what
about the other one, huh? The angel?

25:31.446 --> 25:33.823
[sighs] You don't know the whole story.

25:36.660 --> 25:39.746
Ejllael and I are not only different,
we're also on very bad terms.

25:39.829 --> 25:42.624
You and I are also on very bad terms.

25:44.793 --> 25:46.920
[sighs] Why are you lowering your voice?

25:47.003 --> 25:49.422
Even for Satan,
this isn't a laughing matter.

25:51.132 --> 25:53.885
Ejllael and I fought a long war
against each other.

25:55.595 --> 25:57.430
It was a devastating war.

25:58.181 --> 25:59.516
Why did you two go to war?

26:02.727 --> 26:05.438
-[thunderclap]
-[dramatic orchestral music plays]

26:08.024 --> 26:10.151
[Iblis] He created the angels from light.

26:11.278 --> 26:13.655
And the genies were made
from smokeless fire.

26:17.325 --> 26:20.787
The genies created from fire
became increasingly arrogant.

26:21.371 --> 26:23.748
They had ambitions
to become greater than Him.

26:26.334 --> 26:31.339
In his rage, He sent the angels
and ordered them to exterminate us.

26:34.092 --> 26:35.385
[water gurgling]

26:37.971 --> 26:40.974
[dramatic orchestral music continues]

26:54.279 --> 26:58.116
The angels came down and began
slaughtering all of the genies on earth.

26:58.700 --> 27:02.078
And Ejllael, he led the charge.

27:07.167 --> 27:10.128
The war lasted almost 300 years.

27:10.920 --> 27:12.714
I lost most of my brothers in the fight.

27:14.758 --> 27:18.053
You turned a petty fight
into a 300-year war?

27:18.553 --> 27:20.597
I've barely seen my brothers since then.

27:22.349 --> 27:25.352
I had defied His orders, so as punishment,
I was sent to Hell.

27:26.561 --> 27:30.398
And when I was released, I got stuck in
a lamp for 1,000 years. So, you know.

27:33.526 --> 27:35.570
Where are your surviving brothers now?

27:38.114 --> 27:39.032
I don't know.

27:39.115 --> 27:41.993
Out in the world, in some pot or a lamp.

27:43.161 --> 27:45.038
Living out the rest of their days.

27:47.082 --> 27:49.125
[Iblis] They might be controlling sleep.

27:56.383 --> 27:58.426
Or tending to the garden of souls.

28:04.724 --> 28:05.850
[water gurgling]

28:07.394 --> 28:09.979
-Or even controlling the rain.
-[rain pattering]

28:12.107 --> 28:13.274
Wait. Controlling the rain?

28:17.737 --> 28:19.739
-Huh?
-Can you find the brother who does that?

28:19.823 --> 28:21.825
-Tell him--
-He's moved to somewhere unknown.

28:22.617 --> 28:25.078
Oh! Sade is calling out. I got to go.

28:25.787 --> 28:27.247
-[pants]
-[whooshing]

28:30.208 --> 28:32.961
Sade isn't looking for you. I can tell.

28:41.010 --> 28:42.679
-[whooshing]
-[Iblis] Phew.

28:43.346 --> 28:45.348
[captivating music plays]

29:03.283 --> 29:04.325
Wow.

29:12.250 --> 29:14.085
[tool whirring]

29:15.920 --> 29:19.048
Hey, miss. Does the owner
of this car live nearby?

29:19.132 --> 29:19.966
Yes.

29:20.049 --> 29:21.468
Total crypto king, huh?

29:22.385 --> 29:23.678
I used to have one of these.

29:24.596 --> 29:25.555
It's a 2024 model.

29:26.264 --> 29:27.724
[tool whirring]

29:27.807 --> 29:30.727
Oh, hey, you! Stop. I said patch the tire.
Why are you removing it?

29:32.729 --> 29:36.775
You need to change it.
Have you even disclosed all of this?

29:36.858 --> 29:38.485
It's a lot. Every customization?

29:38.985 --> 29:41.321
What are you, a cop?
Why would I report that?

29:41.404 --> 29:42.530
Hey, put it back on.

29:46.201 --> 29:49.454
-Where do you live, huh?
-[scoffs] What makes you ask that?

29:50.622 --> 29:51.998
You got the hots for me?

29:52.081 --> 29:54.584
I just have this sense
that you'll die on the way there.

29:54.667 --> 29:56.628
-[scoffs]
-These wheels were customized for you?

29:57.337 --> 29:59.631
The tire sizes are wrong.
If I just fix the hole,

29:59.714 --> 30:01.925
it won't last an hour
before it breaks away.

30:02.008 --> 30:05.512
I've explained it to you now.
Call a tow truck to take it out of here.

30:05.595 --> 30:06.638
I refuse to fix it.

30:07.722 --> 30:10.517
You treat your clients this way?
Hey, come here.

30:10.600 --> 30:11.893
[footsteps approaching]

30:14.145 --> 30:15.688
[whimsical music plays]

30:19.651 --> 30:22.487
[exhales contentedly] Is everything okay?

30:23.363 --> 30:25.406
Did you just drink that?

30:25.490 --> 30:27.826
There's still a lot left.
These are for us, aren't they?

30:28.409 --> 30:30.745
[sighs] That's why they keep going fast.

30:31.913 --> 30:34.082
Oh, so what were you saying?

30:35.083 --> 30:37.627
Uh, I need the tow truck's number, please.

30:38.211 --> 30:43.258
0-1-0-6-3-4-2--

30:43.341 --> 30:45.718
Please wait. I couldn't catch that.
[chuckles nervously]

30:47.387 --> 30:48.638
You hit him or something?

30:48.721 --> 30:50.682
[burps, exhales]

30:50.765 --> 30:51.891
[bubble pops]

30:51.975 --> 30:52.809
Whoa.

30:53.476 --> 30:56.771
6-3-4… [sighs]

30:58.731 --> 31:01.609
You're ruining the vibe!
This isn't a little kid's birthday party!

31:02.193 --> 31:03.903
I'll report everything. I'm so very sorry.

31:03.987 --> 31:05.947
-Thank you.
-[Sade] Where are you going?

31:06.030 --> 31:07.824
-Why is he leaving? Don't go.
-Oh, shit!

31:07.907 --> 31:08.992
[staff] Hello, ma'am.

31:13.246 --> 31:14.122
Hello, ma'am.

31:16.374 --> 31:20.003
Who's in charge of the display here?
Tell me, who's in charge here?

31:20.712 --> 31:23.298
-Uh… Oh, she's here!
-[pants] I'm here. I'm sorry.

31:23.381 --> 31:26.342
I ran quickly.
I had to just go out for a second.

31:26.426 --> 31:28.720
I'm having tummy issues again. [laughs]

31:28.803 --> 31:31.848
What makes you think that's an excuse
to leave your station?

31:33.308 --> 31:35.310
We all get sick when we get to our age.

31:35.393 --> 31:37.520
You want to keep your job,
just do it! Is that hard?

31:39.731 --> 31:42.066
-[staff] Uh…
-I won't put up with this.

31:43.568 --> 31:45.570
Ms. Jung Yeong-sun, what did you just say?

31:46.946 --> 31:50.533
I won't put up with it anymore.
I'm fed up with you so I'm quitting.

31:50.617 --> 31:52.535
Your behavior lately has been crazy.

31:52.619 --> 31:54.537
Have you let that promotion
get to your head?

31:54.621 --> 31:55.788
Ms. Jung Yeong-sun!

31:55.872 --> 31:57.540
I don't know how you got that promotion,

31:57.624 --> 32:00.001
but who do you think you are
treating people like this?

32:00.668 --> 32:02.462
There are rumors
that you're taking bribes.

32:02.545 --> 32:05.089
-That true? You think we're stupid?
-Okay, okay.

32:05.173 --> 32:06.633
[Yeong-sun breathing heavily]

32:06.716 --> 32:09.594
[Im-seon breathing heavily]
I was such a fool.

32:10.178 --> 32:12.680
How could I ask to be a branch manager
at this age?

32:13.222 --> 32:15.767
Everyone looks down on me,
and I'm bad at the job.

32:15.850 --> 32:17.769
-[breath trembling]
-[chuckles softly]

32:20.897 --> 32:22.774
I should've become manager sooner.

32:23.358 --> 32:25.693
[pants] Hey, you! Here.

32:26.653 --> 32:27.904
Here's my second wish.

32:28.655 --> 32:32.450
Take me to 20 years ago.
I want to be manager then.

32:33.409 --> 32:37.705
[gasps] If I became branch manager then,
how much would I have made?

32:39.082 --> 32:41.334
[laughs] Mmm.

32:42.794 --> 32:44.087
[chuckles softly]

32:46.255 --> 32:49.217
Then back we go?
To 20 years before?

32:50.218 --> 32:51.177
[chuckles]

32:55.390 --> 32:57.392
[enchanting choral music plays]

33:07.652 --> 33:08.945
[music fades]

33:09.028 --> 33:11.489
BRANCH MANAGER KANG IM-SEON
CHEONGPUNGHO MART

33:11.572 --> 33:13.157
-[gasps]
-[cell phone ringing]

33:14.909 --> 33:17.954
Once you walk through that door,
it will be 20 years in the past,

33:18.037 --> 33:20.123
and you'll still work as the manager.

33:21.165 --> 33:23.167
-[chuckles softly]
-[cell phone ringing]

33:29.674 --> 33:30.591
Yes, hello?

33:40.935 --> 33:44.313
[ominous music plays]

33:56.951 --> 34:00.204
Why are you here alone? Where's your dad?
He said he was going to get you.

34:00.913 --> 34:02.457
Well, Papa has work to do.

34:06.878 --> 34:10.256
It's been a while.
Do you still drink chamomile tea?

34:10.339 --> 34:14.177
Yeah, I continue to be a psychopath,
so caffeine's not for me.

34:14.260 --> 34:16.888
[laughs]

34:17.638 --> 34:18.931
Some people never change.

34:19.599 --> 34:21.601
I thought you'd at least ask
what I'm doing here.

34:22.351 --> 34:24.145
I live here now, with my wife and kid.

34:24.729 --> 34:27.398
We just bought a house.
You put this area on our radar.

34:29.901 --> 34:33.196
I've never told you
exactly where I happen to live.

34:33.780 --> 34:36.657
It's not every day that a fellow alum
opens her own garage.

34:36.741 --> 34:37.909
Oh.

34:38.785 --> 34:42.080
Anyway, it's nice to see you again.
Looks like you're doing well.

34:42.622 --> 34:43.790
And the garage is okay?

34:47.710 --> 34:49.212
[Ka-young] This is true joy.

34:52.423 --> 34:53.883
[Sade growling]

34:54.842 --> 34:56.260
[growling]

34:57.762 --> 34:59.764
[gentle music plays]

35:05.019 --> 35:07.897
This house is the same
as it was 20 years ago.

35:11.150 --> 35:12.318
Except for you.

35:12.401 --> 35:13.653
[rock thudding]

35:28.292 --> 35:30.002
[breath trembling]

35:33.923 --> 35:35.049
[sighs]

35:36.259 --> 35:39.637
In 20 years, you're going to grow up
to be really pretty.

35:40.638 --> 35:42.890
So try not to hurt yourself.
Scars last forever.

35:45.476 --> 35:46.352
[gasps]

35:48.229 --> 35:51.315
-Whoa, what is it?
-Oh, weird memory just resurfaced.

35:54.152 --> 35:54.986
[Iblis] Hmm?

35:56.070 --> 35:58.489
I promised Grandma
to never speak with strangers.

36:00.950 --> 36:02.910
-Go away!
-Ow!

36:02.994 --> 36:04.954
-No!
-Whoa, are you okay?

36:05.037 --> 36:06.122
[sighs]

36:06.205 --> 36:08.499
You haven't changed at all,
as odd as ever.

36:09.041 --> 36:11.043
-[laughing]
-[sighs]

36:12.044 --> 36:15.006
[Sade] "You haven't changed at all,
as odd as ever." [laughs mockingly]

36:15.089 --> 36:16.090
[scoffs]

36:16.799 --> 36:20.136
He was sleazy as hell. Tell me again,
how did you cut your head?

36:21.095 --> 36:22.180
[Iblis] Tsk.

36:23.222 --> 36:25.308
Who do you think did it? [sighs]

36:25.391 --> 36:27.351
Twenty years before, she was even worse.

36:27.435 --> 36:29.437
Did you go to the past
to grant a wish for someone?

36:30.021 --> 36:31.772
-[Iblis] Hmm.
-[rain pattering]

36:31.856 --> 36:33.482
-[thunder rumbling]
-[Iblis] Hmm?

36:34.942 --> 36:35.776
[gasps softly]

36:36.527 --> 36:37.361
[gasps loudly]

36:38.446 --> 36:39.363
[gasps]

36:39.447 --> 36:40.781
[brushing vigorously]

36:40.865 --> 36:42.200
[ominous music plays]

36:45.494 --> 36:47.163
[thunderclap]

36:49.874 --> 36:52.752
That… that'll be 13 bucks.

36:53.920 --> 36:54.754
[beeps]

36:55.838 --> 36:58.216
[cashier] I do need to see
your ID for alcohol.

37:02.887 --> 37:03.888
[fighting noises]

37:03.971 --> 37:05.097
OUT OF ORDER

37:05.181 --> 37:07.516
[chiptune music playing
over arcade machine]

37:17.818 --> 37:20.071
Miss Ki. Is something wrong?

37:22.323 --> 37:23.783
The rain has come.

37:25.076 --> 37:26.244
Have a good night.

37:27.620 --> 37:29.622
[thunder rumbling]

37:35.002 --> 37:36.671
[yelling] Where the hell is he?

37:39.882 --> 37:42.260
-[rain stops]
-[thunder stops]

37:42.343 --> 37:45.096
Why? Why is it doing this?
Why is it stopping?

37:46.180 --> 37:47.515
It's rainy season!

38:00.987 --> 38:02.947
Where were you? It rained tonight!

38:03.030 --> 38:05.908
Do you know how long I searched
the neighborhood looking for you?

38:05.992 --> 38:10.538
Jeez. Hey. You took
a rock this big and you--

38:11.247 --> 38:14.000
Wow. I mean, I heard you were "odd,"
but that's just--

38:14.083 --> 38:16.210
You're changing the subject
as a defense tactic.

38:16.294 --> 38:19.005
By the way, who's the dope that went
and visited you at the garage?

38:19.797 --> 38:21.549
I heard you were kiki-ing together.

38:22.133 --> 38:24.385
You can kiss me or beat me up.

38:24.468 --> 38:26.595
But you can't do both, you kissing maniac!

38:26.679 --> 38:29.223
That right? Then I'm beating you up.

38:30.266 --> 38:32.059
-Get over here.
-Hey, wait.

38:32.143 --> 38:34.353
-You're my master.
-[dog barks]

38:35.855 --> 38:37.481
Shush, you! We're talking right now!

38:38.149 --> 38:40.026
Listen, treat your Genie with care.

38:40.109 --> 38:41.861
-Be nice to me, okay?
-[barking]

38:41.944 --> 38:42.903
I told you to shush!

38:42.987 --> 38:45.990
Jeez, why do all the dogs here
bark like that when they see you?

38:46.073 --> 38:48.492
-[barking]
-They're worried I might take them in.

38:49.535 --> 38:52.997
They rely on reading human feelings
and expressions, and I don't have any.

38:53.080 --> 38:55.499
Look, you! I have no desire
to take you in!

38:55.583 --> 38:57.209
[barking]

39:02.923 --> 39:04.550
[pants, growls]

39:04.633 --> 39:06.469
[continues barking]

39:09.055 --> 39:09.972
Sade!

39:10.056 --> 39:11.265
[sniffing]

39:13.309 --> 39:14.602
[mysterious music plays]

39:14.685 --> 39:15.686
[dog whines]

39:17.355 --> 39:18.856
I'm a spirit of the lamp, a Genie.

39:18.939 --> 39:20.733
[sped-up] I'll grant
three wishes. Make them.

39:20.816 --> 39:22.985
No bringing back the dead,
no traveling to the future.

39:23.069 --> 39:25.196
Anything other than that,
your wish is my command.

39:27.031 --> 39:29.283
[normal voice] First, though,
and pass this on

39:29.367 --> 39:30.993
to the other dogs in the neighborhood.

39:31.077 --> 39:32.620
Stop barking at Ka-young.

39:32.703 --> 39:34.789
If they keep barking even one more time,

39:34.872 --> 39:37.166
I'll turn every last one of you
into a cat.

39:38.209 --> 39:39.085
Go on, say it.

39:40.836 --> 39:43.089
[barking, growling]

39:43.172 --> 39:44.715
[mouthing] Ki Ka-young.

39:45.216 --> 39:46.550
[continues barking]

39:46.634 --> 39:48.469
[growls, meows]

39:48.552 --> 39:52.264
MUTT (AGE 7), MAY 16, 2024
MADE ITS FIRST WISH

39:52.348 --> 39:54.433
TO BECOME A PERSON, WITH SPECIFICS

39:54.517 --> 39:57.395
CHARMING MIDDLE-AGED MAN IN HIS 40S
WHO LOOKS LIKE DANIEL HENNEY

39:58.020 --> 40:00.022
Wow. That's not a face you often see here.

40:00.106 --> 40:01.982
[chuckles] Are they shooting?

40:02.775 --> 40:04.693
You know how I was sad
about losing my eyesight?

40:04.777 --> 40:07.363
-Yeah.
-I'm not worried anymore. [chuckles]

40:07.446 --> 40:09.031
-[chuckles] Let's go then.
-Yeah.

40:09.532 --> 40:10.908
[woman chuckles] Wow.

40:12.493 --> 40:14.495
[upbeat music playing]

40:28.717 --> 40:30.678
[women gasping]

40:30.761 --> 40:32.054
I'm so hungry.

40:32.138 --> 40:33.139
Galbi?

40:33.222 --> 40:35.433
Sounds good. Okay, let's go.

40:35.516 --> 40:37.309
-[gasps]
-[passerby gasps]

40:38.561 --> 40:41.063
Nice hair, nice suit. So handsome.

40:41.647 --> 40:44.525
He's coming toward us.
Do you have makeup in your bag?

40:46.986 --> 40:48.028
[sniffs]

40:48.112 --> 40:49.405
[sniffing]

40:52.700 --> 40:54.034
[sniffing]

40:54.118 --> 40:55.327
[woman gasps]

40:56.787 --> 40:57.913
[continues sniffing]

40:59.707 --> 41:01.208
[comical music plays]

41:01.292 --> 41:03.502
-[gasps]
-[man] Gross, what's he doing?

41:03.586 --> 41:04.628
[woman] He must be crazy!

41:04.712 --> 41:05.838
-[barks]
-[woman] Disgusting!

41:05.921 --> 41:08.674
I've heard the handsome ones
are either dogs or gay.

41:08.757 --> 41:11.093
Well, with how he's acting…

41:12.261 --> 41:13.596
he's clearly a dog.

41:15.181 --> 41:16.682
[objects thudding, clattering]

41:18.058 --> 41:18.893
[Ejllael sighs]

41:24.523 --> 41:26.066
You don't have any water here.

41:33.157 --> 41:34.700
Eat the food tomorrow morning.

41:35.326 --> 41:38.329
[groans, mutters indistinctly]

41:40.289 --> 41:41.165
What?

41:44.877 --> 41:48.255
I don't like the food you give us.
It tastes stale.

41:48.881 --> 41:49.715
[laughs]

41:50.508 --> 41:52.510
Oh, you're saying
it has no flavor. [chuckles]

41:53.135 --> 41:55.221
I could've been heavier-handed
with the salt.

41:55.304 --> 41:57.014
[strained laughing]

41:58.015 --> 42:00.559
It was a joke. [chuckling]

42:01.519 --> 42:05.397
What else does life have in store for me?

42:05.481 --> 42:08.817
Mmm. I'm tired
of that question. [chuckles]

42:11.153 --> 42:12.905
There's one thing I know for certain.

42:13.864 --> 42:15.699
I'll be saving on the cost of salt.

42:15.783 --> 42:18.369
[foreboding music plays]

42:29.713 --> 42:31.715
[tool whirring]

42:37.680 --> 42:39.890
-[blows]
-[cell phone vibrating]

42:42.476 --> 42:43.352
Hi, Grandma.

42:43.936 --> 42:46.605
Ka-young, sweetheart,
you're not seeing things again, are you?

42:46.689 --> 42:49.692
You're taking your medication
and not missing any doses?

42:49.775 --> 42:52.152
Yeah, I'm taking medication
every day. Why?

42:52.236 --> 42:54.989
And if you have any wishes,
you'll tell me about them, right?

42:55.072 --> 42:58.075
-I'll get them for you.
-Wha-- Wishes?

42:58.158 --> 43:01.036
I found this notebook in your room.
What is it? Did…

43:01.120 --> 43:02.788
Did you have a crush on Daniel Henney?

43:04.456 --> 43:06.542
You can… see that?

43:08.127 --> 43:09.295
She's able to see that?

43:10.170 --> 43:11.213
[Iblis] Huh.

43:11.297 --> 43:14.049
Was it always visible to everyone else?

43:14.133 --> 43:15.676
You're seriously asking me that?

43:15.759 --> 43:18.470
[sighs] This stupid magic
is too complicated.

43:19.888 --> 43:21.140
This isn't going to work.

43:21.223 --> 43:23.684
We need a place that's safe and private
to hide the notebook.

43:24.435 --> 43:28.105
Your lamp. No one but you and Sade
are able to get into the lamp, right?

43:28.188 --> 43:32.151
[inhales sharply] If they really
wanted to, Ejllael or Irem could.

43:32.234 --> 43:33.485
You can't enter alone.

43:33.569 --> 43:34.987
Which means it's safe.

43:36.363 --> 43:39.158
What does it look like inside?
Is it warm and cozy?

43:39.241 --> 43:41.243
[clicks tongue, sighs]

43:41.994 --> 43:43.037
It's dismal.

43:43.537 --> 43:44.371
[clicks tongue]

43:57.509 --> 43:58.344
Mmm.

44:04.642 --> 44:08.062
You get it now? Can you picture
how lonely I was in here?

44:08.145 --> 44:09.772
I was trapped for 983 years.

44:09.855 --> 44:11.815
I'm sorry, but I don't feel loneliness.

44:13.275 --> 44:14.652
Are you able to feel sorry?

44:15.653 --> 44:16.528
Of course not.

44:17.321 --> 44:20.407
I say the word "sorry" to be considerate.
Min-ji told me that.

44:22.701 --> 44:24.411
You know what consideration is?

44:24.495 --> 44:27.456
Yes. That one's easy.
As long as I'm honest, it's fine.

44:28.248 --> 44:32.044
For example, I might say something like
this. That relative of yours said that

44:32.127 --> 44:35.464
if you bow your head to a righteous human,
he'll slit your throat.

44:36.131 --> 44:37.049
Ejllael, that asshole!

44:38.133 --> 44:40.636
[scoffs] You think that was considerate?
That's a big threat.

44:41.261 --> 44:44.682
I can't believe it. [exhales]
I'm not scaring you at all.

44:44.765 --> 44:47.101
If I'm being honest,
I don't know what fear is.

44:47.184 --> 44:49.436
Grandma said apathy
is the worst quality in a person.

44:50.979 --> 44:55.484
My grandma is a safety net to my apathy,
and if that safety net…

44:57.694 --> 45:01.740
were to disappear, then I might become
my most violent self.

45:01.824 --> 45:05.327
I'm preparing for that possibility.
You probably know that from spying.

45:06.286 --> 45:08.330
[Iblis] You want to make your death
seem natural.

45:08.997 --> 45:10.165
[hesitates] Of course I know.

45:10.249 --> 45:12.334
It'll be as close
to a natural death as possible.

45:12.418 --> 45:14.420
Like some equipment malfunction at sea.

45:16.130 --> 45:19.800
But what's the point if you don't have
any affection for humans?

45:19.883 --> 45:22.719
Growing up, I learned I'm a stone
in everybody's shoe.

45:24.054 --> 45:25.722
I make people uncomfortable.

45:26.306 --> 45:28.434
So when I remove myself, the stone's gone.

45:29.768 --> 45:30.727
For Grandma's sake.

45:33.480 --> 45:36.650
Kill me if you're going to, and make it
quick. Don't get your throat slit.

45:41.697 --> 45:42.656
Ejllael?

45:43.782 --> 45:46.743
The more I see that angel,
the more he sucks.

45:47.327 --> 45:50.956
-You can't ever lose to him, okay?
-So you're going to take my side now?

45:51.707 --> 45:53.500
-I can't do that?
-No, you can't!

45:53.584 --> 45:55.878
If you help me win, then… [sighs]

45:56.712 --> 45:57.588
When I…

45:59.590 --> 46:00.757
kill you…

46:00.841 --> 46:02.468
Be so strange.

46:02.551 --> 46:04.011
We're beyond strange already.

46:04.887 --> 46:07.306
We're both considered anti-social.

46:07.389 --> 46:10.058
Why do I get the finger-pointing
when everybody loves you?

46:14.021 --> 46:16.940
So what was even the point
of bringing us back together again?

46:20.110 --> 46:21.069
You're right.

46:24.114 --> 46:26.533
That's something
I should've thought about.

46:27.326 --> 46:28.952
At least you seem to understand.

46:31.705 --> 46:33.040
Let's bring furniture. All right.

46:33.999 --> 46:36.960
We'll put the table and chairs
I made in the workshop here.

46:37.044 --> 46:38.045
[sighs heavily]

46:40.422 --> 46:41.840
[lively orchestral music plays]

46:43.967 --> 46:45.302
[whooshing]

46:48.931 --> 46:50.682
They look like you bought them in a store.

46:51.350 --> 46:52.726
I can't believe you created these.

46:53.310 --> 46:55.771
No matter which way
you look at them, the details…

46:55.854 --> 46:59.399
Will you stop talking?
Furniture count, two.

47:01.735 --> 47:03.946
A rug over here would be nice,
wouldn't it?

47:04.821 --> 47:05.656
[scoffs]

47:18.460 --> 47:19.628
Closer, closer.

47:21.296 --> 47:22.172
[Iblis] Hmm?

47:24.508 --> 47:26.677
[automated voice]
Starting the cleaning cycle.

47:32.558 --> 47:33.559
[Iblis] What's this for?

47:34.226 --> 47:37.604
Is it used to fix things,
or maybe to destroy things?

47:38.397 --> 47:39.731
That's up to you, I guess.

47:40.607 --> 47:41.441
[lid thuds]

47:42.150 --> 47:43.527
Hey!

47:45.529 --> 47:48.699
You can't re-enter if you go that way.
It'll take longer than 1,000 years.

47:49.866 --> 47:50.784
That thing.

47:50.867 --> 47:52.160
[vacuum whirring]

47:53.036 --> 47:54.037
[chuckles sheepishly]

47:57.249 --> 47:59.001
[Ka-young] It looks
a little bit nicer now.

47:59.710 --> 48:00.794
I'm feeling better.

48:04.214 --> 48:06.049
Let's talk about Ms. Im-seon.

48:07.301 --> 48:10.345
She could have wished for anything.
She chose a promotion.

48:11.138 --> 48:13.974
What's with the supermarket
that makes her unable to leave?

48:14.600 --> 48:15.976
Humans are like that.

48:16.893 --> 48:20.063
They don't have the confidence to be kings
outside of their own castles.

48:20.689 --> 48:24.651
They only want to rule what they already
know, so that's what they wish for.

48:25.694 --> 48:27.863
It's one of the most
pathetic human traits.

48:28.405 --> 48:30.324
And the reason I hate them all.

48:30.907 --> 48:32.200
-[book thuds]
-[scoffs]

48:34.369 --> 48:36.413
[Ka-young] Mmm. Mmm.

48:40.083 --> 48:43.378
He knows so much,
but understands so little.

48:45.088 --> 48:46.381
Humans hate you too, you know.

48:46.465 --> 48:50.093
[nervously] Ah, so that's the other
use for that. [chuckles nervously]

48:51.470 --> 48:55.474
If I kill you on behalf of all humans,
would that ensure I go to Heaven?

48:56.558 --> 48:58.185
You think you would end there?

48:58.977 --> 49:00.729
He'd give you Heaven if you asked.

49:01.438 --> 49:02.689
Come here, now!

49:03.940 --> 49:05.275
Come on, show yourself!

49:05.359 --> 49:08.153
-I'm going to get you! Get here!
-Ooh! [laughs]

49:08.779 --> 49:10.864
-[Ka-young shouting indistinctly]
-[Iblis laughing]

49:10.947 --> 49:12.616
-[Ka-young] Get over here.
-No way.

49:13.158 --> 49:15.077
[indistinct shouting]

49:16.745 --> 49:18.705
[muffled shouting]

49:18.789 --> 49:20.707
Where is that weird sound coming from?

49:20.791 --> 49:23.627
[muffled shouting continues]

49:23.710 --> 49:26.004
What's this? The sound's coming from here?

49:26.672 --> 49:28.965
-This a radio?
-[muffled shouting]

49:29.049 --> 49:32.052
[Heung-rye] Pan-geum, you here?
Pan-geum, are you home?

49:32.135 --> 49:33.887
-Hello!
-Yes, Seongnim!

49:34.388 --> 49:35.514
-[rumbling]
-[Pan-geum] Whoa!

49:35.597 --> 49:38.100
You came all this way
when it's raining so much?

49:40.310 --> 49:42.104
[Iblis breathing heavily]

49:46.274 --> 49:47.275
The rain.

49:49.319 --> 49:50.529
I heard her say it's raining.

49:51.154 --> 49:52.447
[soft music plays]

49:53.448 --> 49:55.867
That sounds right, doesn't it?

49:56.868 --> 49:58.161
Is there alcohol here?

50:01.289 --> 50:02.124
I could get it.

50:04.876 --> 50:06.670
Couldn't we both go together?

50:08.839 --> 50:10.048
Be quicker if we do.

50:12.175 --> 50:14.970
-Do you have money for the alcohol?
-You pay with this.

50:15.053 --> 50:16.847
-[Pan-geum sobbing]
-Oh, as collateral?

50:17.472 --> 50:20.016
-I wanted to tell you as soon as I heard.
-Grandma?

50:20.100 --> 50:21.435
[sobbing]

50:22.519 --> 50:26.022
Grandma! Why are you crying?
What happened?

50:26.106 --> 50:28.150
-[sobs] What do we do?
-Why is my granny crying?

50:28.233 --> 50:31.403
We just heard
Mr. Kim, the craftsman, has died.

50:31.486 --> 50:34.573
He was the man, the man who taught you
how to carve wood.

50:35.657 --> 50:37.325
Okay, but why is Grandma crying?

50:37.409 --> 50:39.870
A man passed away, so she's sad.

50:39.953 --> 50:42.330
She's sad because he was her friend.

50:42.414 --> 50:45.917
This is exactly why, you know,
why you get called a psychopath.

50:46.001 --> 50:47.210
-Seongnim!
-Oh?

50:47.961 --> 50:50.088
Oh! Oh, my! Oh, no!

50:50.672 --> 50:53.842
My goodness.
Death makes it all seem meaningless.

50:54.342 --> 50:57.220
[both sobbing]

50:58.138 --> 51:03.018
[Heung-rye] It brings out all of the…
all of the tears! [wails]

51:03.643 --> 51:05.645
-[indistinct chatter]
-[people crying]

51:13.487 --> 51:14.446
[Pan-geum sniffles]

51:18.992 --> 51:20.994
[Pan-geum] Oh, my. Oh, goodness.

51:21.661 --> 51:24.039
It's so awful. I can't bear it.

51:24.122 --> 51:27.000
The world casts away someone like him.

51:27.083 --> 51:29.085
[Chang-sik sighs] Well, even so,

51:29.836 --> 51:32.380
he passed comfortably,
as if he were sleeping.

51:32.464 --> 51:33.965
That must be considered a good death.

51:34.049 --> 51:37.010
That's a myth. There's no such thing
as having a good death.

51:38.094 --> 51:41.640
You kids have no idea,
you still have so many years before you.

51:44.476 --> 51:46.520
[Pan-geum] I have no fear
when it comes to dying.

51:47.312 --> 51:50.690
But, when I… I think of Ka-young…

51:50.774 --> 51:52.400
[sobbing]

51:54.027 --> 51:56.613
I worry that my heart will stop beating
because of…

51:57.322 --> 51:59.574
a heart attack.
Or what if I have a stroke?

52:00.242 --> 52:03.620
What if I get cancer and diabetes,
and end up with dementia?

52:03.703 --> 52:06.832
Oh! I would only burden her!

52:07.415 --> 52:09.417
How will she ever take care of me?

52:09.501 --> 52:11.503
Why would you say something like that?

52:12.504 --> 52:16.466
It was in that moment, I realized
she read the exact same articles I did.

52:17.092 --> 52:21.263
"The Rapidly Growing Aging Society."
"Getting Ready for Age-Related Illnesses."

52:22.639 --> 52:23.849
"Medical Tomorrow."

52:24.766 --> 52:26.518
If Grandma dies, I have to die too.

52:26.601 --> 52:31.147
Yet, Grandma, she wants to live
a long and pain-free life.

52:31.857 --> 52:33.233
So, what are you saying?

52:36.069 --> 52:37.571
I am ready to make my second wish.

52:41.658 --> 52:43.076
I want Grandma young.

52:43.159 --> 52:45.871
So make Pan-geum my exact age.

52:47.664 --> 52:48.498
That's it.

52:49.291 --> 52:51.084
This will be the second wish.

52:53.003 --> 52:53.837
[gasps softly]

52:53.920 --> 52:56.089
[upbeat dance music playing]

52:59.759 --> 53:01.636
[music continues]

56:27.926 --> 56:28.927
[music ends]
